WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:06.130
"The situation is under control" – a reassuring
message from the Congolese government, after

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:11.669
it mistakenly announced on Saturday that there
had been another volcanic eruption near the

00:00:11.669 --> 00:00:13.190
eastern city of Goma.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:18.470
The false alarm came only a week after Mount
Nyiragongo roared back to life – forcing

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.320
hundreds of thousands of people to flee the
area.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:30.900
Now, some are braving the return home.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:36.760
More than a thousand volcano refugees left
a camp in Rwanda on Saturday and queued at

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:42.590
the border of the Democratic Republic of Congo
in the hope of a return to normal life once

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:43.590
more.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:48.739
But slowly returning to the city of Goma,
many people no longer have anywhere to call

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:57.570
home – after the Nyiragongo volcano roared
back to life several days ago.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:03.680
Africa's most active volcano saw terrified
people flee the Congolese city as rivers of

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:10.440
lava killed dozens of people and left tens
of thousands homeless.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:16.439
Fears that Mount Nyiragongo could become active
again days after the initial eruption sparked

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:19.631
a mass evacuation of more than half of Goma's
neighborhoods.

00:01:19.631 --> 00:01:25.240
The metropolis is home to about 1.5 million.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.850
People have sought shelter wherever they could,
including school classrooms.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:33.920
Many said they were struggling to find enough
food and water as the United Nations called

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.890
for aid and warned about the risk of cholera.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:40.930
However, not everyone fled the area - frontline
healthcare workers stayed behind to care for

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.120
their patients.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.909
This new mother was in labour when the alarm
was sounded once more.

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:51.310
"We took an oath to remain by our patients'
side.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:56.600
We couldn't run away and follow those who
fled, we had to first observe and see who

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:02.170
among the population would be the last to
leave and see if we were going to flee if

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:06.280
the situation got more complicated."

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:15.590
The natural beauty of Mount Nyiragongo betrays
its volatile nature – leaving thousands

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:18.510
to pick up the pieces and rebuild their lives.

